        ": دَخَلْتُ عَلَى أَبِي عَبْدِ اَللَّهِ عَلَيْهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ وَ أَنَا أُرِيدُ أَنْ أَسْأَلَهُ عَنِ اَلصَّلاَةِ فَبَدَأَنِي فَقَالَ «إِذَا لَقِيتَ اَللَّهَ عَزَّ وَ جَلَّ بِالصَّلَوَاتِ اَلْخَمْسِ لَمْ يَسْأَلْكَ عَمَّا سِوَاهُنَّ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.615 - It is narrated from 'Aidh al-Amasi that He said:\n\"I entered upon Imam Jafar ibn Muhammad Al-Sadiq (as) with the intention of asking him about prayer.\nImam (as) began speaking before I could ask and said: 'If you meet Allah (swt), the Mighty and Majestic, with the five daily prayers, He will not ask you about anything else.'\"."
        ]
      }
